; The other shape of multi-label public suffix: github.io is itself a public
; suffix, so user.github.io is the organizational domain and a sibling
; other.github.io is a *different* organization.
;
; This matters for CAA tree climbing and for any "is this the apex" logic — a
; resolver that naively strips one label lands on github.io and would happily
; read a policy belonging to nobody.
$ORIGIN user.github.io.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN A    198.51.100.95

@       IN CAA  0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
; Quoting is load-bearing: ";" unquoted starts a zone-file comment, which would
; silently produce a CAA record with empty rdata instead of a deny-all.
@       IN CAA  0 issuewild ";"
